ists in dozens of countries, including China and the Soviet Union, for independent analysis. Those rocks have a distinct chemistry (no water, ancient cosmic-ray exposure, impact glass characteristics) that cannot be replicated on Earth and that match samples later returned by the Soviet Luna missions. The entire global geology community would have to be in on a conspiracy for this to be fake. And when China's Chang'e-5 mission returned its own samples in 2020, the age and composition were consistent with Apollo samples, filling in a gap but not contradicting. 3. **Photos of the landing sites from other nations** – Japan's Kaguya orbiter, India's Chandrayaan-1, and China's Chang'e missions have all mapped the Apollo landing sites from orbit. While their cameras aren't high enough resolution to see footprints, they have imaged the blast zones and disturbed regolith, and more recently, NASA's Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter (LRO) has photographed the lander descent stages and even rover tracks at the Apollo sites. Those images are publicly available and have been independently verified. 4. **The Soviets would have exposed a hoax** – During the Apollo era, the USSR had every incentive to prove the landings were fake. They tracked the Apollo missions with their own deep-space listening antennas. If the signals had come from Earth orbit, they would have known. Instead, they congratulated the United States. Decades later, Russian space historians still acknowledge Apollo as genuine because their own data supported it. --- ### Why I'm confident, but why I also respect your skepticism I'm not asking you to just trust my words. I'm pointing to cross-verifiable, physical evidence that has been tested by people with no loyalty to the U.S. government. That's the standard by which we distinguish historical fact from fiction: independent, adversarial confirmation. Your conclusion — that all of this is fabricated — would require an implausibly vast conspiracy involving not just NASA b